<resources>
    <color name="widget_background">#FBF7F1</color>
    <color name="widget_accent">#2E7D32</color>
    <color name="widget_text_primary">#1C1B1F</color>
    <color name="widget_text_secondary">#6E6A63</color>
    <color name="widget_today_background">#2E7D32</color>
    <color name="widget_on_today">#FFFFFF</color>
    <color name="widget_weekend_text">#B3261E</color>

    <!--
        The three dimmed day figures (FD-07).

        These used to be `primaryText.copy(alpha = …)` computed in Kotlin, which had two costs: the
        alpha could not survive a night-mode switch (see below), and a colour could not be asserted.

        **They are now real resources, which means they are resolved by the launcher against its own
        configuration at bind time.** Before this they were literals baked into the composition, so a
        night-mode switch invalidated the whole `RemoteViews` and rebuilt it — the "restart" the report
        describes. There is a night variant of each.

        Each is `widget_text_primary` composited over `widget_background` at the alpha its name
        records, so they can be recomputed by hand if either of those two changes:

            day_out_of_month   primary at 38%   (the dimmed Hijri figure of a neighbouring month)
            day_gregorian_sub  primary at 60%   (the Gregorian day under an in-month Hijri figure)
            day_out_faint      primary at 24%   (the Gregorian day of a neighbouring month)

        A test asserts every colour resolves to a *different* value under `values-night`; it cannot
        assert the value itself, since that would only prove the XML says what the XML says.
    -->
    <color name="widget_day_out_of_month">#A6A3A1</color>
    <color name="widget_day_gregorian_sub">#757373</color>
    <color name="widget_day_out_faint">#C5C2BF</color>
    <color name="widget_arrow_dimmed">#8F8B85</color>
    <!--
        The cell divider (FD-04), off by default. A hairline rather than a full border because the
        grid is 42 cells: a visible border on each would make the month look like a spreadsheet, and
        on a `previewLayout` the framework cannot draw a per-cell separator without 42 more views.
    -->
    <color name="widget_cell_border">#1F000000</color>
    <!-- The ring around a tapped day (FD-09). A ring rather than a fill, so "selected" and "today"
         stay distinguishable on the rare day that is both. -->
    <color name="widget_selected_day">#2E7D32</color>
</resources>